        "id": 35583,
        "name": "Smilinbrax",
        "username": "Smilinbrax",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/2acd7d/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-08-01T22:51:39.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;awp832&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"awp832\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I’m torn on this one.    My tendency is to say that sidekicks are something to be avoided.   In general, sidekicks were a thing of 40 years ago.    Now adays sidekicks are out,   a forgotten relic and painful reminder of when superheroes were posterboys for cheesy dialogue and campy visual effects.    I don’t think we want to bring that into SotM in a meaningful way.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Wait… You mean sentinels is a serious superhero game? I guess nobody sent me the press release. Especially since there are some campy cards already. Hippo man anyone? (at least the new edition will change the creepy aspect of that card).</p>\n<p>Sentinels definitely doesn’t take itself too seriously and that’s part of its charm. I think there is room for sidekicks. Not all of them have to look like 50’s Robin. Dr. strange always had a rotating group of assistants who were not kids.</p>",
